<task id="041" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Reshape IInvoiceAi to capability methods; consumer-type keys</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes a PublicContracts facade (ADR-013) that four later tasks build on; adds Action-backed dispatch consumers (ADR-043 seam test required).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural facade contract (four capability methods, DTO shapes, failure semantics) that 042, 047, 075 and 131 consume; a wrong shape propagates.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff, ai, public-contracts</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add four Action-backed capability methods to IInvoiceAi — ClassifyAsync, CodeLinesAsync, DraftRulesAsync, DraftFirmNoticeAsync — as thin wrappers over IActionResolver plus IActionRunner keyed by new consumer-type constants, with typed request and result DTOs and Null peers, copying CommunicationTriageAi. Keep GenerateEmbeddingAsync, GetPlaybookByNameAsync and GetStructuredCompletionAsync unchanged (042 and 050 retire the old members); ReadInvoiceAsync is task 043's.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Spaarke AI PublicContracts facades, the linear Action runner (ADR-039 / ADR-043) and xUnit seam tests. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>IInvoiceAi, InvoiceAi and NullInvoiceAi expose the four new methods; ConsumerTypes.cs declares InvoiceClassify "invoice-classify", InvoiceLineCode "invoice-line-code", BillingRuleDraft "billing-rule-draft", InvoiceFirmNotice "invoice-firm-notice"; DTOs live in PublicContracts; unit tests and one ADR-043 seam test pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-52 / spec MUST rules: every prompted AI step runs as an Action + Binding through IActionRunner behind IInvoiceAi, model by tier, no by-name playbook lookup, no C# output schemas. Today IInvoiceAi (IInvoiceAi.cs:31-86) exposes only GetPlaybookByNameAsync (:44), GetStructuredCompletionAsync (:62) and GenerateEmbeddingAsync (:81); InvoiceAi wraps IPlaybookService + IOpenAiClient. ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync is NOT on IInvoiceAi — it is on IInvoiceAnalysisService (Services/Finance/IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs:33) and is retired by 050. Spec §11 row "IInvoiceAi capability methods" says reshape, not a new facade.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IInvoiceAi.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/InvoiceAi.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/NullInvoiceAi.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerTypes.cs (constants only — NOT the All list, see constraints)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/InvoiceAiContracts.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/CommunicationTriageAi.cs:70-123 (resolve Action, BoundInputs with OperandChannel.Input, LinearRunContext, RunAsync, parse)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/LinearConsumers/IActionRunner.cs:55 (BoundInputs overload)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AnalysisServicesModule.cs:588 (NullInvoiceAi) and :1402 (InvoiceAi) registrations</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs:251-262 (ConsumerTypes.All vs Binding rows reconciliation)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/InvoiceAiCapabilityTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Finance/InvoiceAiActionSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Ai/ContextBinderActionRunnerSeamTests.cs (real ActionRunner with a fake IOpenAiClient)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/CommunicationTriageAiInputTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No prerequisites. The Actions and Bindings themselves arrive in 042, 047, 075, 131.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, including the PublicContracts facade rule and the publish-size measurement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / ADR-039">Each new InvoiceAi method resolves its Action only through IActionResolver.ResolveAsync with its ConsumerTypes constant and runs it only through IActionRunner.RunAsync (BoundInputs overload). No IPlaybookService, no IOpenAiClient, no prompt text, no output JSON schema and no deployment name in C# for these methods.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-46 fail-closed">In InvoiceAi, a missing Binding or Action, a completion failure or an output that does not parse into the DTO raises a typed exception carrying a stable reason code (ai.invoice.binding_missing, ai.invoice.completion_failed, ai.invoice.output_invalid) after logging identifiers only. Never return a fabricated default and never fall back to a hard-coded prompt. Reuse an existing exception type if one fits; otherwise add exactly one exception type in PublicContracts and justify it in notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">NullInvoiceAi implements every new method with the existing P3 shape (log, throw FeatureDisabledException with ErrorCode ai.invoice.disabled), matching its current methods.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 boot reconciliation">Add the four constants to ConsumerTypes.cs but do NOT add them to ConsumerTypes.All: RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck turns /healthz Unhealthy for any All entry without a Binding row. Each Action task adds its own constant to All in the same change that seeds its Binding (042, 047, 075, 131).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Logs carry identifiers, sizes, timings and reason codes only — never document text, line narratives or model output.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">PublicContracts DTOs do not reference Services/Finance types (Finance consumes the facade, not the reverse). Do not change ActionRunner, IActionRunner, BoundInputs or LinearRunContext.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>AI capability wiring</topic>
