    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Action-backed facade method" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/CommunicationTriageAi.cs">Copy TriageAsync lines 70-123 for the resolve/bind/run/parse sequence; differ only in fail-closed exception semantics (triage degrades to null; invoice capabilities throw typed).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor FULL. Read IInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAi.cs, NullInvoiceAi.cs, CommunicationTriageAi.cs and spec FR-21, FR-22, FR-27, FR-46, FR-50.</step>
    <step order="1">Define DTOs in InvoiceAiContracts.cs. Classify: request (document text, tenant id); result mirroring today's Finance ClassificationResult fields (classification InvoiceCandidate / NotInvoice / Unknown, confidence, hints vendorName / invoiceNumber / invoiceDate / totalAmount / currency / matterReference, reasoning) so 042 maps one-to-one. CodeLines: request (line chunk with line key, date, type, narrative, hours, amount, codes as billed; allowed task / activity / expense codes each with description and guidance text; tenant id); result per line (line key, task / activity / expense code, confidence, observations of type BlockBilling or VagueDescription with confidence and quoted text). DraftRules: request (document text, document id, closed list of billing rule types with their parameter schemas, tenant id); result (proposals with rule type, parameters JSON, consequence, clause quote, clause location; not-converted items with text, location, reason). DraftFirmNotice: request (outcome kind SubmissionRejected / ReturnedToFirm / InvoiceRejected / ApprovedWithAdjustments, structured findings summary, tenant id); result (subject, body prose) with no numeric fields (FR-50).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the four constants to ConsumerTypes.cs with XML docs naming the facade method and the Action task that seeds the Binding.</step>
    <step order="3">Extend IInvoiceAi and InvoiceAi (inject IActionResolver, IActionRunner, logger); implement each method per the reference; serialize the request as the Input operand JSON; parse the JsonElement into the DTO.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend NullInvoiceAi with the four methods.</step>
    <step order="5">Unit tests (mock IActionResolver / IActionRunner) per method: operand carries the request fields; output parses; missing Binding, runner failure and malformed output each raise the typed exception with its reason code; Null peer throws ai.invoice.disabled.</step>
    <step order="6">Seam test under tests/integration/seam/Finance/: ClassifyAsync through the REAL ActionRunner with a fake IOpenAiClient capturing the request — proves the operand reaches the prompt and the structured output reaches the DTO (fails if either is stubbed).</step>
    <step order="7">Run the ArchTests (ADR013_AiBoundaryTests, ADR013_LinearConsumerBoundaryTests, Adr032/GateCombinationConstructibilityTests) and the full unit suite; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations (DTO shape decisions 047 / 075 / 131 must know) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any method needs a change to ActionRunner, IActionRunner, BoundInputs or LinearRunContext (for example a per-call output-schema override), STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6 — that is a platform dispatch change under ADR-043, not part of this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an ArchTest or the ADR-032 constructibility test fails because of the new InvoiceAi constructor dependencies and the fix would require changing another module's registration gate, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>IInvoiceAi (IInvoiceAi.cs:31) exposes only by-name playbook lookup, raw structured completion and embeddings; CommunicationTriageAi is the Action-backed facade pattern. grep "invoice-classify|invoice-line-code|billing-rule-draft|invoice-firm-notice" in src finds nothing.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, and it is extended: the same IInvoiceAi facade gains methods (spec §11 row "IInvoiceAi capability methods"); no new facade. The DTO file is new because PublicContracts must not depend on Finance models.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>042, 047, 075 and 131 have no MUST-compliant way to call their Actions; Finance keeps calling raw completion with C# prompts and schemas, violating D-52 and success criterion 12.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAi.cs, NullInvoiceAi.cs, ConsumerTypes.cs, InvoiceAiContracts.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/InvoiceAiCapabilityTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Finance/InvoiceAiActionSeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">IInvoiceAi declares ClassifyAsync, CodeLinesAsync, DraftRulesAsync, DraftFirmNoticeAsync, and still declares GenerateEmbeddingAsync, GetPlaybookByNameAsync and GetStructuredCompletionAsync with unchanged signatures and behaviour.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each new InvoiceAi method resolves its Action with exactly its ConsumerTypes constant and calls IActionRunner.RunAsync once with an Input-channel operand containing the request fields (asserted per method).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Binding (resolver throws), runner throws, or output missing a required field — each yields the typed exception with reason code ai.invoice.binding_missing, ai.invoice.completion_failed or ai.invoice.output_invalid respectively; no method returns a default result.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NullInvoiceAi throws FeatureDisabledException with ErrorCode ai.invoice.disabled for each new method.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ConsumerTypes.cs contains the four constants with the exact string values above; ConsumerTypes.All is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The DraftFirmNotice result type has no numeric property; the CodeLines result carries only codes, confidence and observations (no amounts).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seam test drives ClassifyAsync through the production ActionRunner and fails if the operand is not in the rendered prompt or the output is not parsed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep in the new InvoiceAi code finds no IPlaybookService, IOpenAiClient, deployment name or JSON-schema literal used by the four new methods.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADR013_AiBoundaryTests, ADR013_LinearConsumerBoundaryTests and Adr032 GateCombinationConstructibilityTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-21, FR-22, FR-27, FR-46, FR-50; Processing Pipeline "Rules for the AI steps". Registration lines in AnalysisServicesModule (:588, :1402) need no change unless the constructor change requires it. The DTO shapes are a starting contract: 047, 075 and 131 may refine their own DTO when authoring the Action and must keep facade, Action schema and parser in step. ActionRunner $choices enrichment (ActionRunner.cs:379 ResolveLookupChoicesAsync, :426 EnrichOutputSchemaWithResolvedChoices — the spec cites :424) applies automatically to JPS Actions; nothing to add here.
Adversarial review (main session, 2026-10-15): one F3 (retry semantics of binding_missing / completion_failed; seam test mocked an impossible path) fixed in 7ee8a9000 with the K3 optional-string null and K4 docs/FR-50 recursion; remaining K items recorded as "Notes for callers" in notes/041-iinvoiceai-capability-contract.md; platform follow-up #1936. Targeted re-run 37/37.</notes>
